Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: bcm2711-rpi: Give vchiq the codec clocks

bcm2835-codec (a vchiq client) drives the H.264, ISP and VPU-core blocks
through the firmware. Name their clocks on the vchiq node so the driver can
hold them up while it streams, as rpi-hevc-dec does through its own node.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi.dtsi
@@ -120,6 +120,11 @@
 
 &vchiq {
 	interrupts = <GIC_SPI 34 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+	/* Blocks behind bcm2835-codec: H.264 (decode/encode), ISP, VPU core */
+	clocks = <&firmware_clocks 6>,
+		 <&firmware_clocks 7>,
+		 <&firmware_clocks 4>;
+	clock-names = "h264", "isp", "core";
 };
 
 &hevc_dec {
